    "The marketing / account suite catalogue for the visual-parity harness (python3 scripts/visual_parity.py --suite marketing).",
    "Every entry is one Figma frame in file SYQn5hFY8YVQKm3c6rw0eJ: 16 pages on page 'Marketing Website' (468:124) and 19 auth/device",
    "states in section 743:124. `height` is the Figma frame's height, which is the size its reference PNG must have.",
    "",
    "status:",
    "  captured     (default) the route is built; it is screenshotted full-page at 1440 wide and compared.",
    "  unbuilt      the route does not exist. The capture visits `path` and FAILS if it stops rendering the site's 404 view,",
    "               so an unbuilt flag cannot outlive the screen it describes.",
    "  not-rendered the state is designed but deliberately not rendered (a documented deviation). `source_probe` names a file and",
    "               strings it must NOT contain; vp_compare fails if the state has appeared in source without being captured.",
    "",
    "scenario / action are NAMED handlers in scripts/vp_capture_marketing.py (scripted API replies and UI steps); no code lives here.",
    "session: true seeds the browser's non-secret session hint so /account's route guard and navbar see a signed-in visitor.",
    "area groups surfaces into the fix tickets raised from the audit (home, marketing-core, secondary, auth, account)."
